Subject: MLA: optional ring buffer for the DSA indexer key plane (EXL3_MLA_KIDX_RING)

MLA layers with a k-pool indexer (GLM-5.3) keep a per-token [k || gate] plane (k_idx) next to the pooled keys.
That plane is only read to rebuild the pools touched by the current forward pass (its own rows plus at most
kpool - 1 earlier rows of the same page). With EXL3_MLA_KIDX_RING=W (default 0 = off, the full plane) each page
keeps only W slots, shaped (pages, W, idx_dim), token t in slot (t % PAGE_SIZE) % W. W must divide the page size
and be at least kidx_ring_min_rows(kpool) (32 for kpool 4).

The ring is an ordinary paged plane (rotated, tiered, copied and exported with its page). The plane-append and
pool-update Triton kernels take a RING constexpr, and the eager path builds pools from the chunk's own rows
before the ring write reuses the carry slots (_update_pool_plane_local). Speculative forwards of up to 16 rows
are supported; model_init.init checks this, and that the model keeps recurrent state, because partial-page
prompt reuse is refused with a ring. EXL3_KIDX_RING_SHADOW=1 is a debug mode for small caches that keeps full
twin planes and byte-compares every forward.

The design follows vLLM's Glm5NextTailCache (Apache-2.0; see the comments in cache/mla.py). Local design, no
upstream counterpart. Test: tests/modules/mla/test_mla_kpool_ring.py.

